void AbstractParallelizedDecompressor::decompressOne(uint32 pieces) const {
    RawDecompressorThread t(this, 1);
    t.taskNo = 0;
    t.start = 0;
    t.end = pieces;
    RawDecompressorThread::start_routine(&t);

    std::string firstErr;
    if (mRaw->isTooManyErrors(1, &firstErr)) {
        ThrowRDE("Too many errors encountered. Giving up. First Error:\n%s", firstErr.c_str());
    }
}
```

`pieces = mRaw->dim.y`. And `t.end = pieces = dim.y`. Then `decompressThreaded` iterates from `t.start = 0` to `t.end = dim.y`:

```cpp
for (size_t i = t->start; i < t->end && i < strips.size(); i++)
    decompressStrip(strips[i]);
```

Since `strips.size() == dim.y == t->end`, the loop iterates over all strips. If any strip throws, the exception is caught, and `setError` is called. Then `isTooManyErrors(1)` returns true, and `ThrowRDE` propagates up.

So the only way for `decompress()` to succeed is if ALL strips succeed. And if all strips succeed, all pixels are written. So `checkMemIsInitialized` should pass.

